WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.838
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level two.

2
00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:09.977
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.277 --> 00:00:17.747
Unit twenty-two: Microfinance. Today you will use gerunds and infinitives after verbs: risk, enable, help.

4
00:00:18.047 --> 00:00:20.688
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.633 --> 00:00:24.959
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:27.178
Microfinance.

7
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:32.366
Microfinance means small loans and financial services for poor people.

8
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.134
Microfinance helps women start small shops.

9
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.681
Your turn. Say: Microfinance.

10
00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:44.034
Microfinance.

11
00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:45.575
Loan.

12
00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:49.187
Loan means money borrowed that must be repaid.

13
00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:52.096
She used the loan to buy a sewing machine.

14
00:00:52.683 --> 00:00:54.987
Your turn. Say: Loan.

15
00:00:57.833 --> 00:00:58.637
Loan.

16
00:00:59.383 --> 00:01:00.315
Borrower.

17
00:01:01.317 --> 00:01:03.514
Borrower means a person who takes a loan.

18
00:01:04.117 --> 00:01:06.128
Each borrower signs an agreement.

19
00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:08.963
Your turn. Say: Borrower.

20
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:12.685
Borrower.

21
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.358
Interest.

22
00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:18.011
Interest means the extra money paid for borrowing.

23
00:01:18.617 --> 00:01:21.104
The interest on the loan was twelve percent.

24
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:24.183
Your turn. Say: Interest.

25
00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:27.930
Interest.

26
00:01:28.683 --> 00:01:29.661
Repayment.

27
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.068
Repayment means paying back borrowed money.

28
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:36.333
Weekly repayment is easier than one large payment.

29
00:01:36.917 --> 00:01:39.755
Your turn. Say: Repayment.

30
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.520
Repayment.

31
00:01:44.283 --> 00:01:45.575
Small business.

32
00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:50.139
Small business means a company with few workers and little capital.

33
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.365
A small business may sell food or clothes.

34
00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.707
Your turn. Say: Small business.

35
00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:01.044
Small business.

36
00:02:01.783 --> 00:02:02.436
Debt.

37
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.972
Debt means money that a person or company owes.

38
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:08.676
A heavy debt can trap a family.

39
00:02:09.283 --> 00:02:12.040
Your turn. Say: Debt.

40
00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:15.646
Debt.

41
00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:17.512
Regulation.

42
00:02:18.517 --> 00:02:22.606
Regulation means official rules that control an activity.

43
00:02:23.217 --> 00:02:26.458
Regulation protects borrowers from unfair interest.

44
00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.505
Your turn. Say: Regulation.

45
00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:33.565
Regulation.

46
00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:38.308
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:47.259
Visal, a report says 'Microfinance enables families to start businesses, but some borrowers risk falling into debt.' Why 'to start' but 'falling'?

48
00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:58.151
Some verbs take an infinitive (enable someone to, help someone to) and some take a gerund (risk, avoid, suggest, involve).

49
00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.565
How can I remember?

50
00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:13.762
Learn them in pairs: enable + object + to; risk + -ing; help + infinitive or base verb; avoid + -ing; manage + to.

51
00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:17.047
Why does it matter for microfinance?

52
00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:31.379
The benefits are clear: loans help women to expand. The risks are also clear: high interest may involve paying more than expected, so regulation is needed.

53
00:03:32.533 --> 00:03:34.150
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:34.983 --> 00:03:39.108
Grammar focus: Gerunds and infinitives after verbs.

55
00:03:39.408 --> 00:03:40.606
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:41.317 --> 00:03:44.698
Microfinance enables families to start small businesses.

57
00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:47.873
Some borrowers risk falling into debt.

58
00:03:48.783 --> 00:03:51.479
Good regulation helps to protect borrowers.

59
00:03:52.433 --> 00:04:01.369
Enable / allow / help + object + to + verb. Risk / avoid / involve + -ing. Never use 'to' after risk: risk losing, not risk to lose.

60
00:04:02.117 --> 00:04:05.791
Be careful! Don't say: They risk to lose their money.

61
00:04:07.733 --> 00:04:10.197
Say: They risk losing their money.

62
00:04:10.497 --> 00:04:12.253
Risk is followed by -ing.

63
00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:15.649
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:16.433 --> 00:04:18.479
Small Loans, Big Choices.

65
00:04:18.779 --> 00:04:22.729
Microfinance offers a small loan to people that banks usually ignore.

66
00:04:23.733 --> 00:04:27.799
A loan can enable a borrower to buy tools or stock for a small business.

67
00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.214
However, high interest and weekly repayment may risk pushing a family into debt.

68
00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:38.626
Regulation helps to protect each borrower and avoids charging unfair fees.

69
00:04:39.633 --> 00:04:43.421
Used wisely, microfinance can lift families out of poverty.

70
00:04:44.533 --> 00:04:48.407
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:52.411
Microfinance enables families blank start businesses.

72
00:04:52.711 --> 00:04:55.842
A, to. B, for. C, -ing.

73
00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.935
The answer is A: to.

74
00:05:02.083 --> 00:05:04.420
Some borrowers risk blank into debt.

75
00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.129
A, falling. B, to fall. C, fall.

76
00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:13.504
The answer is A: falling.

77
00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:16.650
Money that a person owes is blank.

78
00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:20.533
A, debt. B, repayment. C, interest.

79
00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.741
The answer is A: debt.

80
00:05:26.883 --> 00:05:28.616
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:28.916 --> 00:05:34.473
A, They risk to lose money.. B, They risk losing money.. C, They risk lose money..

82
00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:41.043
The answer is B: They risk losing money..

83
00:05:42.183 --> 00:05:45.379
According to the reading, regulation helps protect each…

84
00:05:45.679 --> 00:05:48.821
A, borrower. B, bank. C, tourist.

85
00:05:52.367 --> 00:05:54.413
The answer is A: borrower.

86
00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.601
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:02.239
What are the benefits and risks of microfinance?

88
00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.562
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:12.862 --> 00:06:37.544
The main benefit of microfinance is that it gives poor families access to credit, so they can start a small business and earn a stable income. It also helps women to gain independence. However, high interest and strict repayment may push some borrowers into debt. Therefore, regulation and financial education are essential.

90
00:06:37.844 --> 00:06:39.657
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:45.896
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and gerunds and infinitives after verbs.

92
00:06:46.196 --> 00:06:51.971
Today's value is social impact. Use your skills and ideas to improve other people's lives.

93
00:06:52.271 --> 00:06:55.295
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:55.595 --> 00:06:57.888
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

